  + [origin] is long-haul project-manager session after IR6 coordination mailbox projection implementation was accepted
  + [purpose] is convert accepted IR6 implementation proof and FSC5 operations safety into a new IR7 readiness surface without authorizing live operations control
  + [reason] is IR6 implementation is complete enough to feed downstream operations dry-run planning, but direct IR7 assignment would be false-ready without a fresh readiness rebake

  = must: preserve accepted IR6 implementation proof pack and completion review as boundary inputs
  = must: preserve FSC5 operations safety pack as the controlling safety boundary for IR7
  = must: preserve post-FSC5 implementation readiness lineage and accepted implementation chunk order as background authority
  = must: create a post-IR6 implementation-readiness authority that opens only IR7 planning and final-slice minting, not operations implementation
  = must: keep IR7 dry-run-only, non-mutating, and unable to perform command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, or live machine control
  = must: distinguish operation request records, dry-run result records, safety classification records, refusal records, human approval records, and completion reviews from live effects
  = must: preserve coordination proof boundaries: claims, mailbox carriers, human overrides, conflict reviews, and completion gates cannot be bypassed by operation requests or dry-run output
  = must: require final IR7 slices before any dry-run simulator implementation, fixture file creation, expected ledger creation, generated output creation, adapter work, dependency changes, or package metadata changes
  = must: route IR7 readiness, final-slice minting, operation safety boundary design, and live-control boundary questions to deeper reasoning
  = should: make later bounded fixture drafting and inert dry-run model implementation GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR7 final slice boundaries are accepted

& [RequiredPostIR6ImplementationChunkSet] is the source-level chunk set for the next development stage
